Based on the extensive investigations during the past decade, EMOFs have demonstrated quite a lot of remarkable features.7 For example, the interpenetration of porous MOFs can subdivide the large cavities into the smaller compartments, and the resultant EMOFs consequently possess high thermal stability and intact frameworks when removing those free lattice molecules from the pores. Next, entanglement is an efficient method to enlarge the internal surface areas and then enhance the sorption capacities of EMOFs. Moreover, the networks of some EMOF materials may also shift with respect to each other to change the size and shape of the channels when the guest molecules were expelled.8
